From cd203773300071814419c99e954c970692d4d05a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 05:02:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Prose build profile: the regular image, plus Prose's packages
 and applications

The image was the minimum profile: Tracker, Terminal, a few tools, no
demos, none of the regular applications, no user software. The prose-*
profiles (prose-mmc is what scripts/build-image.sh builds) take the
regular definitions -- ActivityMonitor, Icon-O-Matic, Mail, MediaPlayer,
People, Screenshot and the rest, the preferences, the demos; what needs
Mesa drops out by build feature -- and add the packages that exist for
arm64 only because prosepkg built them: OpenSSL, xz, zip, unzip, Vision,
Pe, and the first applications from HaikuArchives and haikuports
(ArtPaint, BePDF, Tipster, FontBoy, Filer, TaskManager, CapitalBe,
DeskNotes, Slayer, Lingua, FtpPositive, Bong, HexVexed, Minesweeper,
BeSpider, NetPulse, PecoRename, PhantomLimb, PonpokoDiff, Toner, Wakeup,
CopyNameToClipboard). The host name is "prose".

libmidi.so is built only with the fluidlite build feature, and the regular
image lists it: fluidlite and fluidlite_devel are listed, built by
prosepkg, so the MIDI kit and MidiPlayer are in.

The regular definition added the translators that 0037 had moved into the
minimum one, each twice then; it now adds only the rest (AVIF, ICNS,
JPEG 2000, RAW, WonderBrush).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
